  "system": {
    "biography": "<p><strong>An executive in Ludivenko's Seattle operations</strong> — though he will not admit that, and the runners are not meant to find out at the meet. His real name does not matter.</p><p><strong>The offer:</strong> 20,000&yen; each to make Euphoria disappear before her first Amber Gel appearance. Negotiable — run an <strong>Opposed Negotiation Test</strong> against his <strong>Negotiation 6</strong>, and every net success moves the fee by 1,000&yen; in the winner's favour. The <em>payment plan</em> is not negotiable: half after the abduction, half after Euphoria misses her last scheduled appearance.</p><p><strong>The terms:</strong> take her from her penthouse the following night and hold her three days while the appearances come and go. He wants her kept at the rented Royal Meadows flat so he can watch both the star and the runners — <em>\"you, uhm, chummers can hold the lady anywhere you like, but your payments will be delivered to the rented flat.\"</em> He will repeat that <strong>she must not be harmed</strong>: injured or dead, she is no use for Ludivenko's own ads.</p><p><strong>Playing him:</strong> condescending, especially about questions he thinks are obvious. He answers anything reasonable. If the runners turn violent he runs for the car while the chauffeur and Juan Diablo cover him — and the deal collapses.</p>",
